success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Activate the hidden environment (mount overlays and apply the platform layer)

Usage: nails activate [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (overrides binary-relative discovery)

      --no-preflight
          Skip pre-flight checks (DANGEROUS - expert use only)

      --session <POLICY>
          What to do with the graphical session (default: kill)

          Possible values:
          - kill: Terminate the graphical session before mounting (the secure default)
          - keep: Keep the current session running (mounts only what can be overlaid live)

          [default: kill]

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr: -v for debug, -vv for trace

      --pivot <POLICY>
          How to handle a volume that needs a pivot mount (default: refuse)

          Possible values:
          - refuse: Abort rather than fall back to a pivot mount (the secure default)
          - allow:  Fall back to a pivot mount without asking (degraded security)
          - ask:    Prompt on a terminal before falling back to a pivot mount; refuse without one

          [default: refuse]

  -q, --quiet
          Print only errors and the final result

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use colour

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal, TERM is not `dumb` and NO_COLOR is unset or empty
          - always: Always colour, even when piped
          - never:  Never colour

          [default: auto]

  -y, --yes
          Proceed without confirmation prompts

          Without this flag activation prompts on a terminal and refuses to run without one, so it never ends a graphical session unattended.

      --ascii
          Use ASCII markers instead of Unicode symbols and box drawing

      --nixos-flake <FLAKE_REF>
          NixOS layer: flake reference as <path>#<host> (e.g. /etc/nixos#myhost)

          Only applies on NixOS. When set, this value is passed directly to `nixos-rebuild --flake` instead of auto-detecting the flake path. Supports attribute selection after the `#`.

      --dry-run
          Preview activation steps without making changes

      --json
          Print machine-readable JSON on stdout

      --no-log-file
          Do not write the log file on the hidden volume (diagnostics still go to stderr)

      --overlay-only
          Mount overlays only, skip the platform configuration layer

      --risky-services <POLICY>
          What to do with risky services still referencing a target (overrides the `risky_services` config key)

          Unset: restart when the session is killed, prompt on a terminal otherwise, and refuse a non-interactive run that keeps the session.

          Possible values:
          - restart: Restart them so they no longer reference the decoy
          - skip:    Leave them running; they are reported as surviving writers

      --terminate-processes
          Signal non-service processes (shells, editors, scripts) holding a target instead of aborting

          Off by default: a process with no systemd unit can only be stopped by signal, so activation never signals one and aborts before mounting, listing them. This flag ends them anyway.

      --accept-persistent-decoy
          Accept a persistent decoy posture instead of refusing activation

          By default activation refuses a host that keeps forensic traces on the decoy disk: a persistent systemd-journald journal, or an active rsyslog/syslog-ng/auditd. Records those sinks write before the overlays are mounted survive deactivation and reboot. This flag accepts that risk (and overrides `accept_persistent_decoy` in `nails.toml`).

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

EXAMPLES:
  nails activate                      Mount the overlays and apply the layer
  nails activate --session keep       Keep the current graphical session
  nails activate --overlay-only       Mount overlays, skip the platform layer
  nails activate --dry-run            Preview without changing anything

----- stderr -----
